{"causes": ["The rise of UK rave culture in the late 1980s created a fertile ground for the development of new electronic genres.", "Innovations in music production technology during the early 1990s allowed producers to experiment with complex breakbeats and basslines.", "The influence of hip hop and reggae music on British youth culture provided foundational elements for the sound of drum and bass."], "effects": ["Drum and bass has influenced numerous other genres, including dubstep and trap, leading to the evolution of new musical styles.", "The genre has established a global community of artists, DJs, and fans, fostering cultural exchange and collaboration across countries.", "D&B has transformed club culture and electronic music festivals, becoming a staple in dance music events worldwide."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "uk-rave-culture", "sourceName": "UK Rave Culture", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "drum-and-bass", "targetName": "Drum and Bass", "context": "The UK rave culture of the late 1980s and early 1990s directly led to the emergence of drum and bass as a distinct musical genre."}, {"sourceSlug": "goldie", "sourceName": "Goldie", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "drum-and-bass", "targetName": "Drum and Bass", "context": "Goldie's pioneering work in drum and bass, particularly with his album 'Timeless' in 1995, helped define the genre's sound and aesthetic."}, {"sourceSlug": "movement-festival", "sourceName": "Movement Festival", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "drum-and-bass", "targetName": "Drum and Bass", "context": "The Movement Festival, held in Birmingham since 2006, features drum and bass artists, showcasing its significance in the electronic music scene."}, {"sourceSlug": "hospital-records", "sourceName": "Hospital Records", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "drum-and-bass", "targetName": "Drum and Bass", "context": "Hospital Records, founded in 1996, has played a crucial role in promoting and distributing drum and bass music, contributing to its global reach."}, {"sourceSlug": "bbc-radio-1", "sourceName": "BBC Radio 1", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "drum-and-bass", "targetName": "Drum and Bass", "context": "BBC Radio 1 has been instrumental in broadcasting drum and bass music to a wider audience through its shows dedicated to electronic music."}], "places": [{"name": "Birmingham, United Kingdom", "role": "Cultural Hub"}, {"name": "London, United Kingdom", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Nottingham, United Kingdom", "role": "Major Events"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: drum and bass", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "drum-and-bass"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q188994", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum_and_bass"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "drum and bass contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Drum and bass significantly impacted the global music landscape, influencing many subsequent genres and contributing to a vibrant club culture that has engaged millions worldwide.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-26T01:09:43Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30182278383", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Drum and bass (D&B), also known as drum 'n' bass, is a genre of electronic dance music that emerged in the United Kingdom in the early 1990s. It is characterised by fast breakbeats with heavy bass and sub-bass lines, samples, and synthesizers.", "newValue": "Drum and bass (D&B), a genre of electronic dance music, originated in the United Kingdom in the early 1990s, emerging from the rich cultural tapestry of the British rave scene. Significant figures such as Goldie, Roni Size, and LTJ Bukem were instrumental in shaping its sounds and popularizing the genre, which is marked by rapid breakbeats and deep basslines. The genre's evolution intertwined with the socio-political landscape of the UK, reflecting a fusion of hip hop, reggae, and electronic music that resonated globally, making it a significant force in contemporary music history.

The genre took shape around 1991, coinciding with the rise of the UK rave culture, where DJs began to experiment with faster tempos and diverse musical influences. The establishment of record labels such as Metalheadz and Hospital Records further propelled D&B into the mainstream, with tracks like Roni Size's "Brown Paper Bag" winning a Mercury Prize in 1997. This period saw the birth of iconic events such as the Movement festival in Birmingham, which showcased D&B talent and solidified its place within the electronic music genre. The genre's distinct sound, characterized by its rapid breakbeats (typically between 160-180 BPM) and heavy bass, facilitated a vibrant subculture that engaged audiences in dance clubs and festivals worldwide.

Drum and bass has left an enduring legacy, influencing a plethora of music genres including dubstep, trap, and future bass, while also spawning international scenes in Europe, North America, and beyond. The genre's infrastructure—comprising producers, DJs, and promoters—has fostered a community that thrives on innovation and collaboration. As a result, D&B has not only shaped music but has also contributed to broader cultural movements, with its beats being a staple in film soundtracks, advertisements, and gaming. The genre's adaptability continues to inspire new artists, ensuring its relevance in the constantly evolving landscape of music."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-26T01:09:43Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30182278383", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The rise of UK rave culture in the late 1980s created a fertile ground for the development of new electronic genres.", "Innovations in music production technology during the early 1990s allowed producers to experiment with complex breakbeats and basslines.", "The influence of hip hop and reggae music on British youth culture provided foundational elements for the sound of drum and bass."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-26T01:09:43Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30182278383", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["Drum and bass has influenced numerous other genres, including dubstep and trap, leading to the evolution of new musical styles.", "The genre has established a global community of artists, DJs, and fans, fostering cultural exchange and collaboration across countries.", "D&B has transformed club culture and electronic music festivals, becoming a staple in dance music events worldwide."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-26T01:09:43Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30182278383", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "drum-and-